<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Horn and East Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">British Administration of Eritrea</h1><p class="st-meta">1941 CE – 1952 CE · capital Asmara</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The British military and civil administration of the former Italian colony while the world powers and the UN decided Eritrea's future.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After defeating the Italians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keren">Keren</a> and taking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asmara">Asmara</a> in 1941, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> administered <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-eritrea">Eritrea</a> as occupied enemy territory under the laws of war. The peace treaty of 1947 required <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> to give up its colonies, but the four powers could not agree on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea's</a> fate and referred it to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The British kept much of the Italian administration and allowed political parties, trade unions and newspapers in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigrinya-language">Tigrinya</a> and Arabic. Rival parties formed: the Unionists favoured union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muslim-league-of-eritrea">Muslim League</a> and others independence. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> dismantled and sold some industrial plant. A UN commission visited in 1950, and political violence by shifta bands disturbed the countryside.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In December 1950 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations-general-assembly">UN General Assembly</a> decided that <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-eritrea">Eritrea</a> should be federated with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-democratic-republic-of-ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. British administration ended in September 1952, when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a> federation came into being.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1941 CE – 1952 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Horn and East Africa</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:98.33%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1941 CE – 1952 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Asmara</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Ethiopian Orthodox Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Tigrinya, Tigre, Arabic, English</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/eritrea">Eritrea</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>British Military Administration of Eritrea</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1946&amp;focus=british-administration-of-eritrea" aria-label="British Administration of Eritrea on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5743 1607 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where British Administration of Eritrea lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6063 1863L6063 1863M6063 1863L4997 651M6063 1863L6070 2096"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6063 1863h0M4997 651h0M6070 2096h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6063 1863h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6063 1863h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Asmara. <a href="/atlas?year=1946&amp;focus=british-administration-of-eritrea">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
